Title: Get rid of unwanted splash of color which is not splashColor in Flutter FilterChip widget
Tags: flutter, themes

Question:
I have attached a full code demonstrating the problem where the Chip when pressed for selection shows, momentarily, a Cyan colored background which as for my experiments is not the splashColor. I have tried wrapping the FilterChip with Theme and changing various colors to Colors.transparent but nothing seems to work. Please help me fix this.

The Code:

import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void main() {
  runApp(const MyApp());
}

class MyApp extends StatelessWidget {
  const MyApp({super.key});

  @[user]
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return MaterialApp(
      themeMode: ThemeMode.light,
      theme: ThemeData(
        useMaterial3: true,
        brightness: Brightness.light,
        primaryColor: Colors.red,
        scaffoldBackgroundColor: Colors.white,
        colorScheme: const ColorScheme.light(
          brightness: Brightness.light,
          primary: Colors.red,
          onPrimary: Colors.white,
        ),
      ),
      home: const MyHomePage(),
    );
  }
}

class MyHomePage extends StatefulWidget {
  const MyHomePage({super.key});

  @[user]
  State<MyHomePage> createState() => _MyHomePageState();
}

class _MyHomePageState extends State<MyHomePage> {
  final List<Map<String, String>> _categories = [
    {'label': 'Frequent Bugs', 'icon': '🐛'},
    {'label': 'Slow or Laggy', 'icon': '🏎️'},
    {'label': 'Missing Features', 'icon': '🧩'},
    {'label': 'Hard to Use', 'icon': '💡'},
    {'label': 'Pricing / Value', 'icon': '💰'},
  ];

  final Set<String> _selectedCategories = {};

  @[user]
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    final theme = Theme.of(context);
[truncated]

Answer A:
The cyan is secondaryContainer, the default selected color for a Material 3 FilterChip. With ColorScheme.light it falls back to the default secondary, #03DAC6. When a chip gets selected, the fade starts from that color, because backgroundColor isn't used for the selected state.

So use color instead of selectedColor, so both ends of the fade are yours

color: WidgetStateProperty.resolveWith((states) =>
    states.contains(WidgetState.selected)
        ? theme.colorScheme.primaryContainer.withAlpha(20)
        : null),

Answer B:
The cyan comes from your colour scheme, not from the splash. ColorScheme.light() falls back to the default teal for secondaryContainer, and a Material 3 FilterChip uses that colour when it's selected.

Use ColorScheme.fromSeed instead so every colour is generated from red:

theme: ThemeData(
  useMaterial3: true,
  colorScheme: ColorScheme.fromSeed(seedColor: Colors.red),
),

The cyan flash will be gone, and you can remove the Theme wrapper around the chips.

